idden;">&#8203;</span></p></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:9.33%;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:right;margin:0pt 3pt 0pt 0pt;"> <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_CNY_A-gQXq46QE2po1aRK2pCmQ" contextRef="As_Of_12_31_2025_srt_CounterpartyNameAxis_yxt_ShanghaiChinaEuropeInternationalCultureCommunicationCoLtdMember_ePs81fy4V0aguX44ZbabeQ" decimals="-3" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:OtherLiabilitiesCurrent" scale="3" id="Tc_qFgYXihGU0q23BhY-L6u7g_9_4">1,975</ix:nonFraction></p></td><td style="vertical-align:bottom;white-space:nowrap;width:1.71%;margin:0pt;padding:0pt;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p></td></tr></table><div style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10.0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;margin-top:0pt;min-height:1.19em;position:relative;width:100%;"><div style="background-color:#000000;height:1pt;position:relative;top:0.6em;width:25.0%;border:none;margin:0 auto 0 0;"></div></div><table style="border-collapse:collapse;font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin-bottom:0pt;margin-top:0pt;table-layout:fixed;width:100%;border:0pt;"><tr><td style="color:#202529;font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;vertical-align:text-top;white-space:nowrap;width:18pt;padding:0pt;">(1)</td><td style="padding:0pt;"><span style="color:#202529;font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;">The balance represented a RMB </span><span style="color:#202529;font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;"><ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_CNY_A-gQXq46QE2po1aRK2pCmQ" contextRef="As_Of_12_31_2025_us-gaap_RelatedPartyTransactionsByRelatedPartyAxis_us-gaap_RelatedPartyMember_3gPYeTq0dUKChxkLNSBMSw" decimals="-3" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:OtherReceivablesNetCurrent" scale="3" id="Narr_hOkAjwD_ykitQGqTSG_R2g">2,000</ix:nonFraction></span><span style="color:#202529;font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;"> loan to the related party with an interest rate at Loan Prime Rate (&#8220;LPR&#8221;) issued by China&#8217;s central bank. The Group has collected the repayment from Shanghai Fenghe during the year ended December 31, 2025.</span></td></tr></table><table style="border-collapse:collapse;font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin-bottom:0pt;margin-top:0pt;table-layout:fixed;width:100%;border:0pt;"><tr><td style="color:#202529;font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:9pt;vertical-align:text-top;white-space:nowrap;width:18pt;padding:0pt;">(2)</td><td style="padding:0pt;"><span style="color:#202529;font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;">The advance to Yazhou Wu for the Group&#8217;s operation has been fully collected as of the date of this annual report.</span><span style="color:#202529;font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:9pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;"> </span></td></tr></table></ix:continuation></ix:continuation><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p><ix:nonNumeric contextRef="Duration_1_1_2025_To_12_31_2025_IdHyuBsACECPfitzESJYAw" name="us-gaap:IncomeTaxDisclosureTextBlock" id="Tb_E8fReLT7eU--gSG7VkZ7XQ" continuedAt="Tb_E8fReLT7eU--gSG7VkZ7XQ_cont1" escape="true"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;"><b style="color:#202529;font-weight:bold;">15. TAXATION</b></p><table style="border-collapse:collapse;font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin-bottom:0pt;margin-top:0pt;table-layout:fixed;width:100%;border:0pt;"><tr><td style="color:#202529;font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;vertical-align:text-top;white-space:nowrap;width:18pt;padding:0pt;">(a)</td><td style="padding:0pt;"><b style="color:#202529;font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:bold;">Value Added Tax (&#8220;VAT&#8221;) and Surcharges</b></td></tr></table><div style="margin-top:12pt;"></div><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-indent:0pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">The Group is subject to VAT at the rate of <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_6ae-4zkZ7ke8-jxNWF6KGw" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2025_To_12_31_2025_IdHyuBsACECPfitzESJYAw" decimals="2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="yxt:PercentageOfValueAddedTaxRate" scale="-2" id="Narr_uryLeL8o_0eC33mcoa94rQ">6</ix:nonFraction>% for both corporate learning solutions and other revenues.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;"><span style="display:inline-block;text-indent:0pt;width:18pt;"><b style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:bold;">(b)</b></span>Income Tax</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;"><i style="font-style:italic;font-weight:normal;text-decoration-color:#000000;text-decoration-line:none;">Cayman Islands</i></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-indent:0pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">Under the current laws of the Cayman Islands, entities incorporated in the Cayman Islands are not subject to tax on income or capital gain. Additionally, the Cayman Islands does not impose a withholding tax on payments of dividends to shareholders.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;"><i style="font-style:italic;font-weight:normal;text-decoration-color:#000000;text-decoration-line:none;">British Virgin Islands</i></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-indent:0pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">Under the current laws of the British Virgin Islands, entities incorporated in the British Virgin Islands are not subject to tax on their income or capital gains.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;"><i style="font-style:italic;font-weight:normal;text-decoration-color:#000000;text-decoration-line:none;">Hong Kong</i></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;"><span style="font-weight:normal;">Under the current Hong Kong Inland Revenue Ordinance, the Company&#8217;s subsidiaries incorporated in Hong Kong are subject to a two-tiered profits tax rates regime. Under the two-tiered profits tax rates regime, the first HK</span><span style="font-weight:normal;">$<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_HKD_kLnigQAt6EaITdJB6Llmmw" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2025_To_12_31_2025_srt_StatementScenarioAxis_yxt_FirstTwoMillionOfProfitsMember_us-gaap_IncomeTaxAuthorityAxis_country_HK_ckqrbTW4YEm4k6yTdD0G3Q" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="yxt:ThresholdProfitsInDeterminingTaxRate" scale="6" id="Narr_csJvR0vsIkagohaIvzy-hg">2.0</ix:nonFraction></span><span style="font-weight:normal;"> million of profits of the qualifying group entity will be taxed at </span><span style="font-weight:normal;"><ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_6ae-4zkZ7ke8-jxNWF6KGw" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2025_To_12_31_2025_srt_StatementScenarioAxis_yxt_FirstTwoMillionOfProfitsMember_us-gaap_IncomeTaxAuthorityAxis_country_HK_ckqrbTW4YEm4k6yTdD0G3Q" decimals="4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="yxt:PercentageOfTaxRate" scale="-2" id="Narr_HRsTB086kEuv6g_imMrFUA">8.25</ix:nonFraction>%</span><span style="font-weight:normal;">, and profits above HK</span><span style="font-weight:normal;">$<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_HKD_kLnigQAt6EaITdJB6Llmmw" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2025_To_12_31_2025_srt_StatementScenarioAxis_yxt_ProfitsAboveTwoMillionsMember_us-gaap_IncomeTaxAuthorityAxis_country_HK_ItLf5ksZ9065_u0Peh5bzA" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="yxt:ThresholdProfitsInDeterminingTaxRate" scale="6" id="Narr_-FWp81TwW0SqIZb1DNLyMA">2.0</ix:nonFraction></span><span style="font-weight:normal;"> million will be taxed at </span><span style="font-weight:normal;"><ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_6ae-4zkZ7ke8-jxNWF6KGw" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2025_To_12_31_2025_srt_StatementScenarioAxis_yxt_ProfitsAboveTwoMillionsMember_us-gaap_IncomeTaxAuthorityAxis_country_HK_ItLf5ksZ9065_u0Peh5bzA" decimals="3" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="yxt:PercentageOfTaxRate" scale="-2" id="Narr_zGQD3RjtSkeb_5arA10MWA">16.5</ix:nonFraction>%</span><span style="font-weight:normal;">.</span></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;"><i style="font-style:italic;font-weight:normal;">PRC</i></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-indent:0pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">On March&#160;16, 2007, the National People&#8217;s Congress of PRC enacted a new Enterprise Income Tax Law (&#8220;new EIT law&#8221;), under which Foreign Investment Enterprises (&#8220;FIEs&#8221;) and domestic companies would be subject to enterprise income tax at a uniform rate of <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_6ae-4zkZ7ke8-jxNWF6KGw" contextRef="Duration_3_16_2007_To_3_16_2007_yq_Hnu8SHkyhCPqAT82CHQ" decimals="2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:EffectiveIncomeTaxRateReconciliationAtFederalStatutoryIncomeTaxRate" scale="-2" id="Narr_JMk90yfWWkK4nB_3Mp_8QA">25</ix:nonFraction>%. The new EIT law became effective on January&#160;1, 2008. In accordance with the implementation rules&#160;of EIT Law, a qualified &#8220;High and New Technology Enterprise&#8221; (&#8220;HNTE&#8221;) is eligible for a preferential tax rate of <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_6ae-4zkZ7ke8-jxNWF6KGw" contextRef="Duration_3_16_2007_To_3_16_2007_yq_Hnu8SHkyhCPqAT82CHQ" decimals="2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="yxt:PreferentialTaxRate" scale="-2" id="Narr_zXcrmuOJmEK8DWWtDAnoUw">15</ix:nonFraction>%. The HNTE certificate is effective for a period of <span style="-sec-ix-hidden:Hidden_qflLwrxyJkOxHM27cIonaw;"><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;">three&#160;years</span></span>. An entity could re-apply for the HNTE certificate when the prior certificate expires.</p></ix:nonNumeric></div><div style="clear:both;margin-bottom:30pt;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:center;margin:24pt 0pt 0pt 0pt;">F-49</p></div></div>
<div style="background-color:#000000;clear:both;height:2pt;page-break-after:always;width:88.24%;border:0;margin:30pt 5.88% 30pt 5.88%;"></div><div style="max-width:100%;padding-left:5.88%;padding-right:5.88%;position:relative;"><div style="margin-top:30pt;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;"><a href="#TOC"><span style="font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;">Table of Contents</span></a></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;text-align:center;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">YXT.COM GROUP HOLDING LIMITED</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;text-align:center;margin:0pt;">NOTES&#160;TO THE CONSOLIDATED FINANCIAL STATEMENTS</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:center;text-indent:18pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">(All amounts in thousands, except for share and per share data, unless otherwise noted)</p></div><div style="clear:both;max-width:100%;position:relative;"><ix:continuation id="Tb_E8fReLT7eU--gSG7VkZ7XQ_cont1" continuedAt="Tb_E8fReLT7eU--gSG7VkZ7XQ_cont2"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">15. TAXATION (CONTINUED)</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;"><span style="display:inline-block;text-indent:0pt;width:18pt;"><b style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-style:normal;font-weight:bold;">(b)</b></span>Income Tax (continued)</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;"><i style="font-style:italic;font-weight:normal;">PRC (continued)</i></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-indent:0pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">Radnova Intelligence was recognized as a HNTE first time on November 30, 2021 and renewed its HNTE certificate on December 16, 2024, thus it was entitled to the preferential income tax rate of <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_6ae-4zkZ7ke8-jxNWF6KGw" contextRef="Duration_11_1_2021_To_11_30_2021_srt_ConsolidatedEntitiesAxis_yxt_JiangsuRadnovaIntelligenceTechnologyCoLtdMember_JpeA98_un0y2KvBNkbvDIw" decimals="2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="yxt:PreferentialTaxRate" scale="-2" id="Narr_cQx67Fv230qVqCwj6YQ_8g">15</ix:nonFraction>% from calendar year 2021 to 2026. Yunxuetang Information was recognized as a HNTE first time on December 19, 2025, thus it was entitled to the preferential income tax rate of <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_6ae-4zkZ7ke8-jxNWF6KGw" contextRef="Duration_12_19_2025_To_12_19_2025_srt_ConsolidatedEntitiesAxis_yxt_JiangsuRadnovaIntelligenceTechnologyCoLtdMember_rMZBGVn2DEKf-Sp_Ca6GGw" decimals="2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="yxt:PreferentialTaxRate" scale="-2" id="Narr_7z43sBU7DEylzcJugExBRw">15</ix:nonFraction>% from calendar year 2025 to 2027.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-indent:0pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">For qualified small and low-profit enterprises, from January&#160;1, 2023 to December&#160;31, 2027, <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_6ae-4zkZ7ke8-jxNWF6KGw" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2025_To_12_31_2025_IdHyuBsACECPfitzESJYAw" decimals="2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="yxt:PercentageOfAssessableIncomeSubjectToPreferentialRate" scale="-2" id="Narr_W3arPPIZbkiZj8XFhTzG2w">25</ix:nonFraction>% of the first RMB <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_CNY_A-gQXq46QE2po1aRK2pCmQ" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2025_To_12_31_2025_IdHyuBsACECPfitzESJYAw" decimals="-5" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="yxt:FirstThresholdOfAssessableProfitUsedInDeterminingPreferentialTaxRate" scale="6" id="Narr_WSh2ygmvl062TsIELzEKww">3.0</ix:nonFraction> million of the assessable profit before tax is subject to the tax rate of <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_6ae-4zkZ7ke8-jxNWF6KGw" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2025_To_12_31_2025_IdHyuBsACECPfitzESJYAw" decimals="2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="yxt:TaxRateOfAssessableProfit" scale="-2" id="Narr_J95T8k10PUiYpGxmx76G1w">20</ix:nonFraction>%. For the&#160;years ended December&#160;31, 2024 and 2025, there are qualified small and low-profit enterprises in PRC, and thus they were eligible for the above preferential tax rate for small and low-profit enterprises.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-indent:0pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;"><i style="font-style:italic;">Singapore</i></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-indent:0pt;margin:0pt;">The applicable tax rate is <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_6ae-4zkZ7ke8-jxNWF6KGw" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2025_To_12_31_2025_us-gaap_IncomeTaxAuthorityAxis_country_SG_vmEWTGLiGUqhSJFgiPRydA" decimals="INF" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="yxt:PercentageOfTaxRate" scale="-2" id="Narr_ULnbC-Xvc0GxmrkJjlT3Ig">17</ix:nonFraction>% in Singapore, with <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_6ae-4zkZ7ke8-jxNWF6KGw" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2025_To_12_31_2025_srt_StatementScenarioAxis_yxt_FirstTenThousandOfTaxableIncomeMember_us-gaap_IncomeTaxAuthorityAxis_country_SG_NywtrIPXj0yzugiJAyfioQ" decimals="2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="yxt:TaxableIncomeExemptionPercentage" scale="-2" id="Narr_0gbATGSSlEuOcjmrZt05tw">75</ix:nonFraction>% of the first approximately SGD <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_SGD_NAGVhRgtpE2dQn_eVT85kw" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2025_To_12_31_2025_srt_StatementScenarioAxis_yxt_FirstTenThousandOfTaxableIncomeMember_us-gaap_IncomeTaxAuthorityAxis_country_SG_NywtrIPXj0yzugiJAyfioQ" decimals="-3" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="yxt:ThresholdTaxableIncomeForDeterminingExemptionIncome" scale="3" id="Narr_68IyblPp4EuzbZ76aE3qeQ">10,000</ix:nonFraction> taxable income and <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_6ae-4zkZ7ke8-jxNWF6KGw" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2025_To_12_31_2025_srt_StatementScenarioAxis_yxt_NextOneLakhNinetyThousandTaxableIncomeMember_us-gaap_IncomeTaxAuthorityAxis_country_SG_nV8xo7b66EaEtteHRHbAmg" decimals="2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="yxt:TaxableIncomeExemptionPercentage" scale="-2" id="Narr_53-mv8adFUq7YijbA_3ZUQ">50</ix:nonFraction>% of the next approximately SGD <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_SGD_NAGVhRgtpE2dQn_eVT85kw" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2025_To_12_31_2025_srt_StatementScenarioAxis_yxt_NextOneLakhNinetyThousandTaxableIncomeMember_us-gaap_IncomeTaxAuthorityAxis_country_SG_nV8xo7b66EaEtteHRHbAmg" decimals="-3" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="yxt:ThresholdTaxableIncomeForDeterminingExemptionIncome" scale="3" id="Narr_pD50ucd1mEWhWj0TMeSGvg">190,000</ix:nonFraction> taxable income are exempted from income tax.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;"><i style="font-style:italic;font-weight:normal;text-decoration-color:#000000;text-decoration-line:none;">Withholding Tax on Undistributed Dividends</i></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-indent:0pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">The new EIT Law also provides that an enterprise established under the laws of a foreign country or region but whose &#8220;actual management body&#8221; is located in the PRC be treated as a resident enterprise for PRC tax purposes and consequently be subject to the PRC income tax at the rate of <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_6ae-4zkZ7ke8-jxNWF6KGw" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2025_To_12_31_2025_IdHyuBsACECPfitzESJYAw" decimals="2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:EffectiveIncomeTaxRateReconciliationAtFederalStatutoryIncomeTaxRate" scale="-2" id="Narr_-lGhJY-3fEu2df5L3bVuzw">25</ix:nonFraction>% for its global income. The Implementing Rules&#160;of the EIT Law merely define the location of the &#8220;actual management body&#8221; as &#8220;the place where the exercising, in substance, of the overall management and control of the production and business operation, personnel, accounting, property, etc., of a non-PRC company is located.&#8221; Based on a review of surrounding facts and circumstances, the Group does not believe that it is likely that its operations outside of the PRC should be considered a resident enterprise for PRC tax purposes. However, due to limited guidance and implementation history of the EIT Law, there is uncertainty as to the application of the EIT Law. Should the Company be treated as a resident enterprise for PRC tax purposes, the Company will be subject to PRC income tax on worldwide income at a uniform tax rate of <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_6ae-4zkZ7ke8-jxNWF6KGw" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2025_To_12_31_2025_IdHyuBsACECPfitzESJYAw" decimals="2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:EffectiveIncomeTaxRateReconciliationAtFederalStatutoryIncomeTaxRate" scale="-2" id="Narr_wgRWfhaCn0S0OBPwQ3t3hA">25</ix:nonFraction>%.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-indent:0pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">The new EIT law also imposes a withholding income tax of <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_6ae-4zkZ7ke8-jxNWF6KGw" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2025_To_12_31_2025_IdHyuBsACECPfitzESJYAw" decimals="2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="yxt:PercentageOfWithholdingIncomeTaxOnDividendDistributed" scale="-2" id="Narr_Z3bbYXwHXUO6nkdptqqiZQ">10</ix:nonFraction>% on dividends distributed by an FIE to its immediate holding company outside of China, if such immediate holding company is considered as a non-resident enterprise without any establishment or place within China or if the received dividends have no connection with the establishment or place of such immediate holding company within China, unless such immediate holding company&#8217;s jurisdiction of incorporation has a tax treaty with China that provides for a different withholding arrangement. According to the arrangement between Mainland China and Hong Kong Special Administrative Region on the Avoidance of Double Taxation and Prevention of Fiscal Evasion in August&#160;2006, dividends paid by an FIE in China to its immediate holding company in Hong Kong will be subject to withholding tax at a rate of no more than <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_6ae-4zkZ7ke8-jxNWF6KGw" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2025_To_12_31_2025_srt_RangeAxis_srt_MaximumMember_C63pehBeWki2E5FLsOgWmg" decimals="2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="yxt:PercentageOfWithholdingIncomeTaxOnDividendDistributedUponQualifyingHoldingInterestCriteriaForForeignInvestor" scale="-2" id="Narr_vVcyOAtxm0iF4v9n3SdQrw">5</ix:nonFraction>% if the foreign investor owns directly at least <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_6ae-4zkZ7ke8-jxNWF6KGw" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2025_To_12_31_2025_IdHyuBsACECPfitzESJYAw" decimals="2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="yxt:PercentageOfHoldingInterestForReducedWithholdingIncomeTaxOnDividendDistributedForForeignInvestor" scale="-2" id="Narr_YULbw2FJ60GjadujRbidnw">25</ix:nonFraction>% of the shares of the FIE and if Hong Kong company is a beneficial owner of the dividend. The State Taxation Administration (&#8220;SAT&#8221;) further promulgated SAT Public Notice [2018] No.9 regarding the assessment criteria on beneficial owner status.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-indent:0pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">As of December&#160;31, 2024 and 2025, the Group does not have any plan for its PRC subsidiaries to distribute their retained earnings and intends to retain them to operate and expand its business in the PRC. Accordingly, <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_CNY_A-gQXq46QE2po1aRK2pCmQ" contextRef="As_Of_12_31_2025_5IryGwC9oke0aszZ8EaVhw" decimals="-3" format="ixt-sec:numwordsen" name="yxt:DeferredTaxLiabilitiesWithholdingTax" scale="3" id="Narr_YdI4RU0-uECg75kUq_a_fg">no</ix:nonFraction> deferred income tax liabilities on withholding tax were provided as of December&#160;31, 2024 and 2025, respectively.</p></ix:continuation></div><div style="clear:both;margin-bottom:30pt;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:center;margin:24pt 0pt 0pt 0pt;">F-50</p></div></div>
